<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Study Flashcards</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #fff5fb;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #b52d72;
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 15px;
        }

        .card {
            background: white;
            padding: 22px;
            margin: 18px 0;
            border-radius: 15px;
            box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
        }

        .question {
            color: #b52d72;
            font-size: 20px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .answer {
            background: #fff0f7;
            padding: 15px;
            margin-top: 12px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>📖 Computer Science Study Flashcards</h1>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="question">Q1. What is HTML?</div>

        <div class="answer">
            HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language and is used to
            structure content on web pages.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="question">Q2. What is CSS?</div>

        <div class="answer">
            CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets and is used to style
            web pages.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="question">Q3. What is an Algorithm?</div>

        <div class="answer">
            An algorithm is a step-by-step procedure used to solve a problem.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="question">Q4. What is a Database?</div>

        <div class="answer">
            A database is an organized collection of information.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="question">Q5. What is a Variable?</div>

        <div class="answer">
            A variable is a named storage location used to hold a value.
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
